{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:\"10.1021/nl203503s\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"22047401","source":"MED","pmid":"22047401","doi":"10.1021/nl203503s","title":"Direct mechanical measurements reveal the material properties of three-dimensional DNA origami.","authorString":"Kauert DJ, Kurth T, Liedl T, Seidel R.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Kauert DJ","firstName":"Dominik J","lastName":"Kauert","initials":"DJ","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1796-6181"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Biotechnology Center, Technische Universität Dresden, Dresden, 01062, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Kurth T","firstName":"Thomas","lastName":"Kurth","initials":"T","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5624-1717"}},{"fullName":"Liedl T","firstName":"Tim","lastName":"Liedl","initials":"T","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0040-0173"}},{"fullName":"Seidel R","firstName":"Ralf","lastName":"Seidel","initials":"R","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6642-053X"}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5624-1717"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0040-0173"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1796-6181"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6642-053X"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"12","volume":"11","journalIssueId":1889361,"dateOfPublication":"2011 Dec","monthOfPublication":12,"yearOfPublication":2011,"printPublicationDate":"2011-12-01","journal":{"title":"Nano letters","medlineAbbreviation":"Nano Lett","issn":"1530-6984","nlmid":"101088070","essn":"1530-6992","isoabbreviation":"Nano Lett"}},"pubYear":"2011","pageInfo":"5558-5563","abstractText":"The application of three-dimensional DNA origami objects as rigid mechanical mediators or force sensing elements requires detailed knowledge about their complex mechanical properties. Using magnetic tweezers, we directly measure the bending and torsional rigidities of four- and six-helix bundles assembled by this technique. Compared to duplex DNA, we find the bending rigidities to be greatly increased while the torsional rigidities are only moderately augmented. We present a mechanical model explicitly including the crossovers between the individual helices in the origami structure that reproduces the experimentally observed behavior. Our results provide an important basis for the future application of 3D DNA origami in nanomechanics.","affiliation":"Biotechnology Center, Technische Universität Dresden, Dresden, 01062, Germany.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"grantId":"261224","agency":"European Research Council","acronym":"ERC_","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"DNA","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Microscopy, Atomic Force"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Nucleic Acid Conformation"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Motion"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Nanostructures","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"UL","qualifierName":"ultrastructure","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Biomechanical Phenomena"}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"DNA","registryNumber":"9007-49-2"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/nl203503s"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","citedByCount":120,"hasData":"N","hasReference